# QRP reconstruction (post Phase 1)

Before implementing or refactoring a **workspace module**:

1. Read `docs/reference-analysis/` — especially `QRP_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md`, `REFERENCE_COMPONENT_CATALOG.md`, and module stubs under `docs/reference-analysis/repositories/`.
2. Log progress in `docs/reference-analysis/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md` when a phase gate or production API slice lands.

## Hard rules

| Do | Do not |
| --- | --- |
| Pair frontend + backend for the module | Ship list/detail UI on lab-only or 404 paths without documenting gap |
| Use `require_permission` + `get_ctx` on every new route | Unguarded FastAPI routes (startup assert will fail) |
| Honest empty/error when API missing | Fake KPI counts or badge numbers |
| Pattern-only from AGPL/GPL vendors | Copy vendor code into `frontend/src` or `backend/qre` |
| Contextual `WorkflowSteps` on detail/wizard | Global governance step rail on list pages |

## Design

- `docs/product/QRP_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` and `frontend/src/styles/index.css` tokens — no wholesale reskin without user approval.
- `docs/product/QRP_REFERENCE_RECONSTRUCTION_MASTER.md` is the session-level mission prompt.

## Commits

One module vertical slice per iteration when possible (API + tests + doc rows + minimal FE contract fixes).